==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*knehtaz}}, of unknown origin: cognate with Old Frisian ''[[knecht]]'', Old Saxon ''[[kneht]]'', Old High German ''[[kneht]]'' (German ''[[Knecht]]'', Danish {{term|knægt|lang=da}}, Dutch ''[[knecht]]'').

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kniht/|[kniçt]|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|m}}

# [[boy]], [[youth]]
# (male) [[servant]], [[attendant]]
# male of high military rank, ranking below a [[baron]], usually previously having worked as a [[page]] or [[squire]]

====Declension====
{{ang-decl-noun-a-m|cniht}}

